From: oneup03 <oneup03@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:21:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] Link the N64 osGetTime under another symbol on the 3DS

libctru defines osGetTime too, and both end up in the executable.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ultramodern/include/ultramodern/ultra64.h | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ultramodern/include/ultramodern/ultra64.h b/ultramodern/include/ultramodern/ultra64.h
index 31eb106..7858317 100644
--- a/ultramodern/include/ultramodern/ultra64.h
+++ b/ultramodern/include/ultramodern/ultra64.h
@@ -291,6 +291,11 @@ PTR(void) osViGetNextFramebuffer();
 PTR(void) osViGetCurrentFramebuffer();
 u32 osGetCount();
 void osSetCount(u32 count);
+#ifdef __3DS__
+// libctru has its own osGetTime (milliseconds since 2000); the N64 one keeps
+// its declared name for the generated code but links under another symbol.
+#define osGetTime ultramodern_osGetTime
+#endif
 OSTime osGetTime();
 void osSetTime(OSTime t);
 int osSetTimer(RDRAM_ARG PTR(OSTimer) timer, OSTime countdown, OSTime interval, PTR(OSMesgQueue) mq, OSMesg msg);
